Chapter: E1000MdioSlow
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 Intel I219 datasheet rev 2.02 section 9.2 requires reduced MDIO frequency
 mode for register reads, and 9.3 requires the page register to reach the
 bit that turns it on. The arm this runs under refuses reads until it is
 set, exempting only the page register and the mode register itself.

 The reset arm is the one that earns its place. A PHY reset returns the
 paged registers to their defaults, so slow mode set BEFORE the reset is
 gone by the time any read needs it; the driver sets it after, and this
 reads a register that is only reachable if that ordering held.

Section: Fixtures

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  bar-of : PciDevice -> Integer
  bar-of (dev) =
   let enabled = pci-enable-device dev
   in (pci-parse-bar (dev.pci-bus) (dev.pci-dev) (dev.pci-func) 0).bar-base

Section: Judges

 Before any bring-up the mode is at its reset default, so an ordinary
 register read is refused and comes back as the error sentinel.

  read-before-slow : PciDevice -> Boolean
  read-before-slow (dev) =
   let mmio = bar-of dev
   in let r = e1000-reset mmio
   in e1000-phy-read mmio e1000-phy-id1 < 0

 The page register answers while ordinary reads do not. That separates a
 gated bus from a dead one: if this also failed, the arm would be
 indistinguishable from -e1000-no-phy and would prove nothing about pages.

  page-reg-answers : PciDevice -> Boolean
  page-reg-answers (dev) =
   let mmio = bar-of dev
   in e1000-phy-set-page mmio 0 >= 0

 A page nothing is modelled on must answer error rather than zero, the
 same distinction e1000-phy-read-at draws for an unanswered address.

  bad-page-errors : PciDevice -> Boolean
  bad-page-errors (dev) =
   let mmio = bar-of dev
   in let p = e1000-phy-set-page mmio 999
   in let v = e1000-phy-read mmio e1000-phy-custom-mode
   in let back = e1000-phy-set-page mmio 0
   in v < 0

  slow-mode-takes : PciDevice -> Boolean
  slow-mode-takes (dev) =
   let mmio = bar-of dev
   in e1000-phy-slow-mode mmio == 1

 After a full bring-up the ordinary read that failed above succeeds, and
 it succeeds only if slow mode was set on the far side of the PHY reset.

  read-after-bring-up : PciDevice -> Boolean
  read-after-bring-up (dev) =
   let mmio = bar-of dev
   in let r = e1000-reset mmio
   in let b = e1000-phy-bring-up mmio
   in e1000-phy-read mmio e1000-phy-id1 > 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in act
      when e1000-find scan
        is Just (dev) -> act
          print-line-uni ("read before slow : " & yn (read-before-slow dev))
          print-line-uni ("page reg answers : " & yn (page-reg-answers dev))
          print-line-uni ("bad page errors  : " & yn (bad-page-errors dev))
          print-line-uni ("slow mode takes  : " & yn (slow-mode-takes dev))
          print-line-uni ("read after setup : " & yn (read-after-bring-up dev))
        end
        is None -> print-line-uni ("candidate found : no")
    end
  end

